  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected Thursday. Some\ndrought relief is possible, though flooding is not expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure exits across the Maritimes Wednesday night while \nan occluded front approaches from the west. An area of rain will\nbegin to expand eastward across the forecast area Wednesday \nnight in advance of the front. A disturbance moving around an \nupper low across Quebec province will help support a developing \nlow along the front Thursday. Rain will occur regionwide \nThursday, along with the slight chance of an afternoon \nthunderstorm. The developing low will begin to cross the Gulf \nof Maine Thursday night, though the exact track is still \nuncertain. Rain chances will begin to diminish later Thursday \nnight. The surface low exits across the Maritimes Friday, while\nthe upper low crosses the region. Showers will persist across \nthe region Friday, with the better chances across northern \nareas. The surface/upper lows vertically stack across the \nMaritimes Friday night into Saturday, slowing the movement of \nthe system. Shower chances will persist Friday night into \nSaturday. The system then exits Saturday night into Sunday. The \nentire forecast area should receive a soaking rain Later \nWednesday night into Thursday night. However, rain totals are \nstill uncertain dependent on exactly where the surface low \ndevelops and how rapidly the system exits.",
